  faqs: [
    { question: "How do I get matched with an IB tutor in Dehradun?", answer: "Send IB Gram your child's programme, subject, level and exam series, and we shortlist tutors who have actually taught that course before. Because so few Dehradun schools run IB or Cambridge, geography takes a back seat to syllabus fit, and we then check the lesson time against your evenings. A free trial runs online before anything is decided, and a poor fit just gets swapped out." },
    { question: "Does IB Gram cover Edexcel as well as Cambridge IGCSE for Dehradun students?", answer: "Both boards, yes, delivered as online home tuition rather than a visit to the house. Cambridge students are matched down to the code and tier, Mathematics 0580 Extended or Chemistry 0620 for example, and Edexcel students by specification and Foundation or Higher tier, working from each board's own past papers throughout." },
    { question: "Will a tutor actually come to our home in Dehradun?", answer: "No. That kind of visit is something IB Gram runs only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR, nowhere else in the country. In Dehradun, every lesson happens live online, one to one, over video with a shared whiteboard, which is genuine private tuition delivered at home rather than a promise that anyone turns up at your door." },
    { question: "How much does an IB or IGCSE tutor cost in Dehradun?", answer: "It tracks the programme and level, the subject, session length and how recently the tutor taught that syllabus, and we settle a figure for your specific match before the trial runs, not after. HL Diploma work usually costs more than MYP or IGCSE Core. Since everything is online there is no travel charge to fold in, and nothing here runs on a long contract." },
    { question: "Are there schools in Dehradun that actually teach IB or IGCSE?", answer: "Three do: SelaQui International School runs Cambridge alongside CBSE, and both Ecole Globale International Girls' School and Unison World School add Cambridge IGCSE and A Level to their base board. Woodstock School, up in Mussoorie, is the region's one IB World School, authorised for MYP and DP. Dehradun's famous boarding schools, The Doon School and the Welham schools among them, run CISCE instead." },
    { question: "Can we try a class before committing to anything?", answer: "Every match starts that way. Your child works through real syllabus content with the tutor online, free of charge and with zero obligation to continue. A short plan for the first month follows the trial, and only then do you choose to go ahead, ask for adjustments, or request someone else." },
    { question: "Will a tutor write or fix my child's IB Internal Assessment?", answer: "No, though they will guide it closely. That means helping settle on a workable research question, unpacking what each criterion actually rewards, sanity-checking a data-collection plan and giving honest feedback on drafts. Producing or correcting the assessed work itself breaches IB's integrity rules, and that line does not move for any request." },
    { question: "What Diploma subjects does IB Gram actually cover for Dehradun students?", answer: "Given the size of Dehradun's DP cohort, requests cluster around Maths, both AA and AI, at HL and SL, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A and Computer Science, with Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay support running alongside any of these." },
    { question: "What about MYP and PYP, not just the Diploma?", answer: "Covered as well. MYP tutoring in Dehradun usually centres on criterion-based analysis in the sciences and in Language and Literature, plus the Personal Project's process journal. PYP sessions build reading, writing and number confidence, along with the research habits the Exhibition eventually calls for, in short regular online slots." },
    { question: "Given how few local specialists exist, is online tuition actually good enough here?", answer: "It tends to work better than the local alternative, if there even is one. A shared whiteboard, live past-paper work and recorded worked examples replace nearly everything a tutor physically present would do, and the trade-off opens access to specialists anywhere in India rather than whoever happens to live nearby." },
    { question: "How does IB Gram check a tutor before introducing them?", answer: "Qualifications, recent hands-on teaching of that exact subject and level, and their approach to assessment criteria all get checked before any introduction happens. Given how thin Dehradun's own IB and IGCSE base is, someone who has taught the current syllabus recently is prioritised over a generalist. The trial class then lets you confirm that for yourself." },
    { question: "What's the right age or grade to start tutoring in Dehradun?", answer: "Ideally right at the start of the course: Class 11 for the Diploma, Grade 9 for IGCSE, which leaves room to fix gaps before internal exams, IA deadlines and predicted grades arrive. Starting later, even in the final year, can still help meaningfully if the sessions stay narrowly focused on high-value topics and past papers." },
    { question: "We're switching our child from CBSE. What actually needs the most work?", answer: "Usually exam technique rather than raw content knowledge, and that holds for most Dehradun switchers. Command words such as 'explain', 'evaluate' and 'justify' need direct, explicit teaching, and IA or coursework planning habits need building from nothing. Starting over the summer before the switch gives that groundwork time to settle." },
    { question: "Can we schedule around a busy Dehradun school week, including weekends?", answer: "Yes; weekday evenings and weekend mornings are what most families end up booking. Plans account for the monsoon disrupting evening routines, for winter fog pushing early starts later, and for breaks like Dussehra and Diwali. A second weekly slot ahead of mocks is easy to add since everything runs online." },
    { question: "What if the tutor turns out to be the wrong fit?", answer: "Flag it and we sort out someone else. Progress gets checked with every family every few weeks precisely so a mismatch does not run on for months, and nothing here is locked into a long contract that would make pausing or switching difficult." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram connected to any school, or to the IB or Cambridge directly?", answer: "No, and that holds for every school mentioned on this page as well as Cambridge Assessment International Education, Pearson Edexcel and the International Baccalaureate Organization. Naming a school here only describes where a Dehradun family actually studies; tutors still work to that school's calendar and the relevant board's published syllabus." },
  ],

